1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:03,224
Why do you worship a stone along with Tulsi?

2
00:00:03,224 --> 00:00:03,950
And who is

3
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:08,230
that stone? Brahm Vaivarta Purana says,

4
00:00:08,230 --> 00:00:12,840
Tulsi did penance and asked for one boon Narayan as her husband.

5
00:00:12,970 --> 00:00:14,030
But Brahma ji said,

6
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:15,740
[Brahma] First you will be married

7
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:17,670
[Brahma] to Shankhachuda.

8
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:19,648
Shankhachuda was invincible.

9
00:00:19,648 --> 00:00:23,942
Two armors protected him: Krishna's armor and Tulsi's devotion.

10
00:00:23,942 --> 00:00:25,510
The gods were defeated.

11
00:00:25,630 --> 00:00:29,403
Then Vishnu came as an old Brahmin and asked for the armor.

12
00:00:29,403 --> 00:00:31,513
Then, taking Shankhachuda's form,

13
00:00:31,513 --> 00:00:32,600
he went to Tulsi.

14
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:35,599
And at that very moment,

15
00:00:35,599 --> 00:00:37,872
Shiva's trident ended Shankhachuda.

16
00:00:37,872 --> 00:00:40,340
Tulsi realized this is not my husband.

17
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,264
[Tulsi] Your heart is made of stone.

18
00:00:43,264 --> 00:00:44,660
So go, become a stone!

19
00:00:45,590 --> 00:00:47,530
Vishnu did not avert the curse.

20
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:49,761
[Vishnu] On the banks of Gandaki,

21
00:00:49,761 --> 00:00:52,053
I will live as Shaligram. And without you,

22
00:00:52,053 --> 00:00:53,690
my worship will be incomplete.

23
00:00:55,310 --> 00:00:57,553
And Tulsi became the Gandaki river,

24
00:00:57,553 --> 00:00:58,834
and the Tulsi plant.

25
00:00:58,834 --> 00:01:00,628
Tulsi had asked for Narayan,

26
00:01:00,628 --> 00:01:01,910
and she got Narayan.

27
00:01:02,030 --> 00:01:04,009
Just not in the way she thought,

28
00:01:04,009 --> 00:01:05,988
so both are worshipped together.

29
00:01:05,988 --> 00:01:08,090
And on Devutthana, their marriage.

30
00:01:09,650 --> 00:01:11,497
If this story touched your heart,

31
00:01:11,497 --> 00:01:13,680
then follow or subscribe to Naad Katha.

